& [GeneratedBindingFinding] is exact for windows-sys 0.61.2
  + [CreateFileW] is gated by Win32_Security and returns raw HANDLE
  + [GetFileInformationByHandleEx] returns BOOL and accepts class, void pointer, and u32 bytes
  + [GetFinalPathNameByHandleW] returns u32 and accepts WCHAR pointer, u32 characters, and flags
  + [GetVolumeInformationByHandleW] returns BOOL and accepts two WCHAR buffers plus three scalar outputs
  + [GetLastError] returns WIN32_ERROR
  + [FILE_ID_INFO] is u64 volume serial plus 16 identity bytes
  + [FILE_REMOTE_PROTOCOL_INFO] is 116 bytes in the proven target ABI
  + [dependency_features] are already pinned by the no-call compile probe

& [OfficialReturnFinding] fixes causal classification
  + [final_path_zero] is ordinary API failure followed by immediate GetLastError
  + [final_path_at_or_above_buffer] is successful required-size information and maps to returned_length_limit
  + [volume_zero] is not-all-requested-information and maps to query fault with immediate GetLastError
  + [fixed_query_zero] maps to query fault with immediate GetLastError
  + [zero_GetLastError] cannot satisfy the nonzero OS-fault form and maps to invalid_observation

& [OwnershipFinding] is one-way
  + [failure] INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE is rejected before ownership
  + [success] one FromRawHandle transfer creates one OwnedHandle
  + [borrow] every later call uses AsRawHandle while the owner remains live
  + [closure] OwnedHandle drop closes the resource on every Rust return and unwind path
  + [direct_close] is forbidden

& [UnsafeBudgetFinding] is six blocks
  + [block_1] CreateFileW plus immediate failure error capture
  + [block_2] OwnedHandle from_raw_handle transfer
  + [block_3] FileIdInfo query plus immediate failure error capture
  + [block_4] final volume-GUID path query plus immediate failure error capture
  + [block_5] volume-information query plus immediate failure error capture
  + [block_6] remote-protocol query plus immediate failure error capture
  + [module] is one private cfg(windows) module allowed under crate-level deny unsafe_code

